\subsection{Solution of the Baseline SEACLR System via the Homotopy Analysis Method}
\label{sec:HAM}

The baseline SEACLR system~\eqref{eq:model1} is solved using the Homotopy Analysis Method (HAM), a semi-analytical technique for obtaining approximate solutions of differential equations. A semi-analytical approach expresses the solution in an analytical series form while allowing approximation where an exact closed-form solution is difficult to obtain. This is appropriate for the present model because the six compartment equations are coupled and may not admit a simple closed-form solution.

Table~\ref{tab:ham_notation} lists the symbols used in the Homotopy Analysis Method (HAM) and the Homotopy Perturbation Method (HPM). Each one is defined in full where it first appears in the derivation below. None of them is a parameter of the SEACLR model; they belong to the solution technique only.

