\subsection{Selection of the Convergence-Control Parameter}

With constant controls, every correction $\mathbf{x}_m(t)$ is a polynomial in $t$. At $m=1$, equation~\eqref{eq:S_first_deformation} gives
\begin{equation}
	x_{S,1}(t)=\hbar\,\rho_{S,0}\,t,\quad
	\rho_{S,0}=5.26,
	\qquad
	x_{E,1}(t)=\hbar\,\rho_{E,0}\,t,\quad
	\rho_{E,0}=-4.36 .
\end{equation}
These are the first corrections to the unaware ($S$) and exposed ($E$) groups. The term $\rho$ is each group's net weekly loss at launch, losses minus gains. At $\hbar=-1$ the unaware group falls by $5.26$ per week and the exposed group rises by $4.36$. Higher corrections depend on $\hbar$, a tuning setting with no marketing meaning, which is chosen from an $\hbar$-curve.

\begin{figure}[H]
	\centering
	\includegraphics[width=0.85\textwidth]{figures/fig1_hbar_curve.png}
	\caption{Choice of the convergence-control parameter $\hbar$: largest error of the HAM series over 10 weeks for 10, 15 and 20 terms. The green band marks the best region and the star marks the value $\hbar=-0.8$ used for HAM. The dot marks the standard HPM value $\hbar=-1$.}
	\label{fig:hbar_curve}
\end{figure}

Figure~\ref{fig:hbar_curve} plots the largest error over the first 10 weeks against $\hbar$, for series of 10, 15 and 20 terms. Each curve has a flat low region between about $\hbar=-0.9$ and $\hbar=-0.7$, and in this region the error of the 20-term series is below $4\times10^{-7}$. The lowest point moves to the left as terms are added: it lies near $\hbar=-0.72$ for 10 terms, near $-0.84$ for 15 terms and near $-0.86$ for 20 terms.

The standard HPM setting $\hbar=-1$ lies on the steep side of the curves. At 20 terms its error is about $3\times10^{-2}$, against about $1\times10^{-8}$ at the lowest point, a difference of more than six orders of magnitude. To the left of $\hbar=-1$ the error grows rapidly. The error reaches the size of the whole audience ($11.5$ consumers) near $\hbar=-0.9$ for 10 terms, near $\hbar=-1$ for 15 terms and near $\hbar=-1.1$ for 20 terms, and beyond these points the series is unusable. To the right of the best region the error rises slowly, so the choice is less critical on that side.

The value $\hbar=-0.8$ lies in the low region for all three curves and is used for HAM, with an error of about $4\times10^{-8}$ at 20 terms. At this value the first-order corrections become $x_{S,1}=-4.21\,t$ and $x_{E,1}=3.49\,t$.

In summary, the first-order corrections show that, immediately after launch, the susceptible compartment $S$ depletes at the rate $\hbar\rho_{S,0}$ while the exposed compartment $E$ accumulates at the rate $\hbar\rho_{E,0}$. The convergence-control parameter $\hbar=-0.8$, selected from the $\hbar$-curves, yields a 20-term approximation accurate to $O(10^{-8})$, whereas the HPM value $\hbar=-1$ gives only $O(10^{-2})$ at the same number of terms.

